@startuml
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam shadowing false
title JSON-RPC message flow over the language WebSocket
autonumber
hide footbox

actor "Monaco editor" as Editor
participant "AssemblerLanguageClient" as Client
participant "WebSocket /language" as WS
participant "WebSocket handler" as Handler
participant "AssemblerLanguageSession" as Session
participant "sicxe::Assembler" as Assembler

note over Client,WS
One JSON-RPC message is sent in each WebSocket text frame.
This endpoint does not use stdio Content-Length framing.
end note

note over Client,Session
Request:
{jsonrpc:"2.0", id, method, params}

Response:
{jsonrpc:"2.0", id, result} or
{jsonrpc:"2.0", id, error}

Notification:
{jsonrpc:"2.0", method, params}
A notification has no id and receives no JSON-RPC response.
end note

== Initialize: request and response ==
Client -> WS : initialize request (id = 1)
WS -> Handler : text frame
Handler -> Session : handle(request)
Session --> Handler : response with capabilities/catalog
Handler --> WS : JSON-RPC response
WS --> Client : same id = 1
Client -> WS : initialized notification (no id)
WS -> Handler : text frame
Handler -> Session : handle(notification)
note over Client,Session
No response is sent for this notification.
end note
Client -> Editor : install language catalog

== Document notification and diagnostics ==
Editor -> Client : open or change document
Client -> WS : didOpen / didChange notification\n(no id, URI, version, full text)
WS -> Handler : text frame
Handler -> Session : replace document snapshot
Session -> Assembler : assembleDetailed(text)
Assembler --> Session : AssemblyResult
Session --> Handler : publishDiagnostics notification\n(no id, URI, version, diagnostics)
Handler -> WS : send notification
WS --> Client : server notification
Client --> Editor : update Monaco markers
note over Client,Session
didOpen, didChange, didSave, and didClose
are notifications. Diagnostics are a separate
server-initiated notification.
end note

== Language feature: request and response ==
Editor -> Client : completion / hover / definition /\nreferences / rename
Client -> WS : JSON-RPC request (id = 42)
WS -> Handler : text frame
Handler -> Session : handle(request)
opt cached analysis is stale
  Session -> Assembler : assembleDetailed(current text)
  Assembler --> Session : AssemblyResult
end
Session -> Session : compute feature result
Session --> Handler : result or error with id = 42
Handler --> WS : JSON-RPC response
WS --> Client : same id = 42
Client --> Editor : resolve provider request

== Close document ==
Editor -> Client : close document
Client -> WS : didClose notification (no id)
WS -> Handler : text frame
Handler -> Session : erase document
Session --> Handler : publishDiagnostics with empty list
Handler -> WS : send notification
WS --> Client : clear markers

== Protocol errors ==
alt invalid JSON text frame
  Client -> WS : malformed JSON
  WS -> Handler : text frame
  Handler -> Handler : parse fails
  Handler -> WS : parse error with id = null
  WS --> Client : error response
else failed request
  Session --> Handler : error object with request id
  Handler --> WS : JSON-RPC error response
  WS --> Client : same id and error details
end

note over Session,Assembler
The session owns documents and cached analysis.
The assembler supplies source analysis only;
this channel does not execute programs or mutate
Simulator memory, registers, or project state.
end note
@enduml
